{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Ruby missing: no install step before ruby -v",
    "Explanation": [
      "The step list shows only 'Spin up environment', 'Preparing environment variables', 'Checkout code', then 'ruby -v'. The config has placeholder comments ('# Add Orb here', '# Add step below to install Ruby version 2.6.3') with no actual install step, so no Ruby installation was attempted. As a result, `ruby -v` failed with 'command not found' (exit 127).",
      "",
      "The image must stay `cimg/base:stable`, which rules out change_base_image. Increasing the timeout does nothing for a missing binary.",
      "",
      "The config is version 2.1 and has an empty `orbs:` placeholder plus an install-step placeholder. That points to adding the CircleCI Ruby orb (e.g. circleci/ruby) and using its `ruby/install` command with version '2.6.3' before `ruby -v`. Installing via apt would not reliably give exactly 2.6.3 based on these artifacts. So the fix is add_ruby_orb."
