{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow run on branch 'koans-08-branch-filters' finished SUCCESS, with all three jobs green, so the pipeline was green. However, the requirement says `deploy` must run only for commits to the `production` branch. In this run `deploy` executed (its steps, including 'echo \"Deploy complete\"', ran successfully) on a non-production branch. The run therefore violated the requirement.",
      "",
      "The config has no branch filters on any workflow job entry. Relying on `requires` does not restrict branches: deploy simply runs after test-production on every branch. Nothing in the requirement restricts `build` or `test-production`, so only the `deploy` workflow entry needs to change.",
      "",
      "The correct fix is to add `filters: branches: only: production` to the `deploy` entry in the workflow. Branch filters are configured on workflow job entries, not on job definitions. An `ignore` list of non-production branches cannot cover all possible branch names, so it would not reliably enforce the rule. Adding `only: production` keeps the production run green, since build, test-production and deploy would all still run there."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
