{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on untagged branch push",
    "Explanation": [
      "pipeline_green: The workflow `build-test-and-deploy` and all three jobs report SUCCESS, so the run was green.",
      "",
      "behaviour_correct: The run was a branch pipeline (`koans-09-tag-filters`, triggered via API), and the summary shows no tag. `deploy` still ran and succeeded. The requirement says untagged branch pushes must not deploy, so the behaviour is wrong. This happens because `deploy` has no filters and therefore runs on every branch push.",
      "",
      "fix_target_job and fix: By default, CircleCI does not run jobs for tag pushes. A job only runs on a tag if it has an explicit `filters.tags` entry. This also applies to every job it depends on through `requires`; otherwise the dependency is never scheduled and the downstream job never runs. Two changes are therefore needed:",
      "- `deploy` needs `filters: tags: only: /^beta-.*/` together with `branches: ignore: /.*/`. This makes it run only for beta tags and never for branch pushes.",
      "- `build` and `test` also need tag filters, either the same beta regex or a permissive one. Without them, pushing `beta-main-0.1.1` would not run `build` and `test`, so `deploy` would never run and the requirement for a green deploying workflow would fail.",
      "",
      "Because the workflow config of all jobs must change, the target is `all_jobs`. The change is beta-only tag filtering, which rejects `alpha-*` tags."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
