      "workflow.txt shows build-linux, build-mac and build-windows all SUCCESS, so builds_green is true. deploy is FAILED in workflow.txt, and in steps.txt the 'Verify apps present' step FAILED, so deploy_green is false. job.log lists the workspace contents after attach_workspace: only ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt and ./meta/windows/build.txt. No app files were present, and the first `test -f app/linux/app.linux` exited with status 1 under bash -eo pipefail, so workspace_had_apps is false. The cause is in config.yml: each build job's persist_to_workspace lists only meta/\u003cplatform\u003e, never app/\u003cplatform\u003e. The app files are created in each build container but never carried over to deploy. The fix is to add app/linux, app/windows and app/mac to the paths of their respective persist_to_workspace steps (root '.'). Attaching at '.' then places them at app/\u003cplatform\u003e/app.\u003cplatform\u003e, so the verify step passes and store_artifacts uploads them. The other options do not work: putting store_artifacts in the build jobs does not make the files available in deploy, fixing one platform leaves two missing, changing the attach point does not create the missing files, and removing the verify step drops part of the requirement without delivering the apps."
